                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Edit: Now that I've finished the game, I came here to say that I can't recommend it. It's too buggy and too short to be considered finished and the only real challenge here is trying to have a good control over your character. It could be so much more...\n\nA well-designed adventurer with a engaging story, Parvaneh is fun and enjoyable, but it still has to evolve. First of all, it needs a save button or something that indicates when the autosave happens, because I don't know. The game also needs a jump button. There's a lot of adventurers out there that doesn't need one, but it's not the case for this game. Sometimes it's a little hard to control Fadia (the main character), specially when we have to jump across gaps or reach a platform, thus meaning that the game needs to improve its overall mechanics. Also, some of the missions that I've found so far lack a little bit of creativity, so do the enemies. Besides bringing up these problems, I'm really liking it, this game has a world and a mythology of it's own and the devs are clearly putting some effort into bringing an original material.",
